<title>USA: Ohio $65 mln housing deal yields 6.15 pct in 2028.</title>
<headline>Ohio $65 mln housing deal yields 6.15 pct in 2028.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co said Wednesday it tentatively priced $65 million Ohio Housing Finance Agency revenue bonds at a top yield of 6.15 percent in 2028.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>OHIO HOUSING FINANCE AGENCY</p>
<p>RE: $65,000,000*</p>
<p>RESIDENTIAL MORTGAGE REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>(MORTGAGE-BACKED SECURITIES PROGRAM)</p>
<p>NOTE: THE COLUMN HEADINGS FOR THE &quot;PROJECTED WEIGHTED AVERAGE</p>
<p>LIFE (IN YEARS)&quot; FOR THE 2016 TERM BOND AND THE 2019 TERM BOND</p>
<p>ON PAGE 13 IN THE PRELIMINARY OFFICIAL STATEMENT ARE REVERSED.</p>
